<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        This module deliberately contributes NO menus.

        It used to hang a "Swedish Accounting Training" menu under the
        accounting root. That made the module responsible for knowing which
        root the accounting app uses, and the answer changed twice:

          * account_accountant_ce 18.0.1.0.x created its own root
            (account_accountant_ce.menu_accounting) and left the core
            account.menu_finance behind as an empty shell. Parenting the
            training menu to account.menu_finance made that empty shell
            visible again, so users saw two accounting apps.

          * account_accountant_ce 18.0.1.1.0 reversed course and renamed
            account.menu_finance in place instead. The training menu then had
            to move back, because the root it pointed at was deleted.

        A training module has no business tracking the accounting app's menu
        structure. The content stays reachable through the Training Categories,
        All Lessons and Diagnostic Quizzes actions, which are granted to the
        relevant groups in security/ir.model.access.csv. If a menu is wanted,
        install it somewhere that is not the accounting root.

        NOTE ON CLEANUP
        Earlier versions created menu_training_root, menu_training_categories,
        menu_training_lessons and menu_quiz. They are NOT deleted here:
        <delete> on an xmlid that no longer exists raises
        "External ID not found" and aborts the whole upgrade. Odoo also removes
        a module's ir.model.data rows on upgrade when the record is gone from
        the files, so the menus disappear from the UI on their own.
    -->
</odoo>
